\code{sieve_structure_groups()}): each item's target is its facet's factor,
\code{off_construct} names the facet of the strongest other factor, and an item
of the construct without a facet has no target. \code{factor_level} says which
(\code{"construct"} or \code{"facet"}).

With a single construct and no facets the factor analysis has one factor,
so there is no factor other than the target for an item to load on. The off target
loading (\code{loading_off_max}) is then \code{NA}, not zero (zero would read as an
estimate), \code{off_construct} and \code{suggest_construct} are \code{NA}, and
\code{cross_loading} is \code{FALSE}.

The correlation matrix the factor analysis and the redundancy flag read
is the shared basis of the included items when one is supplied (see
\code{sieve_state_basis()}: Pearson for continuous items, polychoric or
tetrachoric for ordered or binary items, the same matrix the
